    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement: on a successful owner create, an audit line is emitted via the logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- In `addOwner(...)`, immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (the point at which the owner has its generated id, customerCode, and rolled registrationDate populated), emit:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nPlacing it after the save guarantees all three values are present (the id is assigned by persistence, and `customerCode` is generated inside `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`). The test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, with the observed line `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-04`.",
